      "suggestedVersionCode": "30",
      "description": "Delhi NCR Metro plans trips across the Delhi Metro and the Noida Metro Aqua Line in one app. The two operators do not share tickets, so a trip that crosses between them shows the walk at Sector 52 and 51 and a separate fare for each.\n\nPlan a trip\n\n* Shortest route and fewest changes, side by side, with time, fare, every station and where to change\n* Weekday and weekend fares, and first and last train times\n* Cross-network trips with a walk leg and split fares\n* Book tickets on WhatsApp from a journey, one step per operator\n* Your planned journeys stay available offline\n\nStations and lines\n\n* Station search by name or code\n* Station pages with gates, lifts, platforms, facilities, parking and nearby places\n* Lines with ordered stations and interchange badges\n\nMap and alerts\n\n* A network map drawn from station coordinates, with pan, pinch zoom and station search\n* The official DMRC and NMRC maps, with save to gallery\n* Service alerts from both operators\n* Lines, stations and alerts stay readable when the network drops\n\nAppearance\n\n* Material You colours, fixed palettes, dark mode and AMOLED black\n* High contrast, haptics, and slide, fade or no page animations\n\nWhy it asks for permissions\n\n* Network, to fetch routes, fares and alerts\n* Photos, to save a network map to your gallery\n\nThe same app runs in a browser at https://ncr-metro.tashif.codes. It is not an official DMRC or NMRC app.\n",
      "issueTracker": "https://github.com/tashifkhan/delhi-metro/issues",
      "license": "MIT",
      "name": "Delhi NCR Metro",
      "sourceCode": "https://github.com/tashifkhan/delhi-metro",
      "summary": "Plan Delhi Metro and Noida Metro trips with fares, maps and alerts",
      "webSite": "https://tashif.codes/projects/delhi-metro",
      "added": 1785013639000,
